  "question": {
    "text": "Two equal sides of an isosceles triangle are along $-x+2 y=4$ and $x+y=4$. If m is the slope of its third side, then the sum, of all possible distinct values of $m$, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hEWv9",
      "text": "$-2 \\sqrt{10}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ZioW1",
      "text": "$12$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rUL3J",
      "text": "$6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "CbyjD",
      "text": "$-6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/SeNBcP9VVg8-b1sjEOAun5T89VdePL9GJbkE4LUiK8U.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nSlope of the third side = slope of the perpendicular bisector of given lines\n$h: \\frac{-x+2 y-4}{\\sqrt{5}}= \\pm \\frac{x+y-4}{\\sqrt{2}}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & h_1: \\sqrt{2}(-x+2 y-4)=\\sqrt{5}(x+y-4) \\\\ & h_2: \\sqrt{2}(-x+2 y-4)=-\\sqrt{5}(x+y-4) \\\\ & M_{L_1}:-\\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}-2 \\sqrt{2}}\\right] \\\\ & M_{L_2}:-\\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}+2 \\sqrt{2}}\\right] \\\\ & M_{L_1}+M_{L_2}=-\\left[\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}-2 \\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{5}+2 \\sqrt{2}}\\right]\\end{aligned}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & =-\\left[\\frac{(\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{5}+2 \\sqrt{2})+(\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{2})(\\sqrt{5}-2 \\sqrt{2})}{-3}\\right] \\\\ & =6\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
